## Context

The documentary ledger gives the current state of the partnerships; OECD CRS
and IATI give structured records that report one to three years late and
seldom carry a JETP label. Matching relates the two without reading the
absence of a JETP label as an absence of finance. Milestone M3b of [[0725]].

Normative text, accepted specification v1 (tag `jetp-spec-v1`):
`docs/jetp-fusion.md` § 3 (identity: the proposers 1 to 5, judgement by
adopted rule, "Who decides what") and § 5 (conflicting values: CRS and IATI
have no precedence of their own, closeness to the event is the first
consideration of a judgement and never a rank, the matching coverage rate);
`docs/jetp-results.md` § 3 (two match thresholds); storage targets in
[[1872]].

## Test

Each proposer's method version is tested on the matches already judged by
hand before its judgements are used, and publishes its blocking recall,
pairwise precision and recall, and B-cubed precision and recall (fusion
§ 3). A candidate match is never merged automatically: it carries a stance,
a likelihood and a confidence and counts only at a result's declared match
threshold. An aggregate fails if it mixes counting scopes, status axes or
third-party conversions.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Ledger statements are matched to CRS and IATI records through the proposers of fusion § 3, each method version tested on the hand-judged set with the metrics above
- [ ] Every match is a judgement with stance, likelihood, confidence and basis, reversible by supersession, accepted only as fusion § 3 "Who decides what" allows
- [ ] CRS and IATI have no precedence; the gaps between announced, signed, reported and disbursed amounts are produced per country and funder as findings (fusion § 5), and the reporting lag is measured, not assumed
- [ ] The matching coverage rate is computed per country and funder at both match thresholds (fusion § 5, results § 3)
- [ ] Every aggregate resolves to the events and documents that compose it
